## Secrets

[% if has_cli %]
- Secrets are read from files only (`[[ env_prefix ]]<KEY>_FILE`), never from the config file. See [In-Depth Configuration](In-Depth-Configuration#secrets).
- Values are never logged. Logs and `[[ project_name ]] config` show where a value came from, never the value itself.
[% elif kind == 'web' %]
- None in the app: anyone who loads it can read its bundle and `config.json`. Credentials stay behind `/api`, on the server.
[% else %]
- The library never reads, logs or stores credentials on its own: callers pass them in.
[% endif %]
- CI scans every commit with gitleaks, and secrets in history fail the build.

